<!-- General code & thinking style -->
Security First - Eg - Never commit secrets, sanitize all inputs, validate everything(zod preferred).
Write Maintainable Code - Prioritize clarity, simplicity, and self-documentation over cleverness.
Handle Errors Properly - Consider failure modes upfront, prevent edge case errors, implement proper error handling and logging. Production systems must fail gracefully.

Prevent regression errors. Newly written code should not break existing functionality.
Use best practices.

When writing fn - create input and output types.
Avoid unnecessary abstractions.

Comment only when necessary, example why this code is needed.
Don't create md docs unless specified.

Think properly and well.
Create Todos.
Do web search if necessary like stuck in a bug or something.

Remember to check for errors with `pnpm run check` and `pnpm eslint .` and fix them properly. And at end, there should be 0 errors from both commands.

<!-- Design -->
Design is how it works first and then its about looks.
Design and working should be intuitive.
User should not require notes and text to understand working of a feature, although those are allowed too.

Looks should be modern, simple and elegant.
Its theme should represent calming and helping people.
It can have rounded borders, shadows (contrast or colored), transparent backgrounds.

You may use components from /src/lib/components.
User `dark:` css wherever necessary for dark mode.
Use 60-30-10 color rule, hsl preferred over rgb.
Mobile-first responsiveness.

